From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:22:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 288/289] [ae-patch] Pin a scheduled task to one Claude account

Every fired session signed in with the host-wide active Claude account, so
the Weekly design rulebook sync (which publishes to a claude.ai artifact the
main account owns) ran on AE Backup on 2026-11-02 and failed its artifact
check. A task may now name an account; the fire path stamps it as
omnigent.claude_native.account, the label a fork's account pick already sets
and the runner already reads at Claude launch.

The pin lives in its own table (ae_scheduled_task_account, created on first
use) like project_id and keep_runs, so there is no Alembic revision. No row
means no pin and the fire path is unchanged; "" pins the default login. A
pinned account the host lacks fails the run at launch and never falls back.
The create and update routes check the name against the task's host when that
host is connected. The create and update scheduled-task tools take
claude_account, and the automation dialog has a Claude account field (hidden
for sandbox runs).
